{"kind":"report","text":"Ruling on 641ba5c6 and supplement 8a13b2ee: R16 adds no revision and no creation family. It enforces reserved paths at the host in every room, and declared prefixes wait.\n\nReserved paths close the harm that the audit found: workflows that run with the room's secrets, and files that the room's rules read as control. Declared prefixes stop one application from overwriting another's files. That harm is smaller, and it does not justify a new Rules install revision, a new Destination revision and a new creation family now.\n\n1. This head does R16 item 1 and the reserved-path half of item 3. In every room, whatever its pins, the host's publication step refuses a path under a reserved path before the provider push. The record is the existing host-refused outcome, as 4fac2158 rules for older pins. The answer names the reserved path.\n2. Reserved paths: `.github/`, and every path that the room's rules or destination read as control. Include the CODEOWNERS locations outside `.github/` (the repository root and `docs/`). List each reserved path in the head report with where it is read.\n3. No package declaration, no publication capability, no new pin and no legacy prefix mapping. Existing packages, and Lending's shelf pages under either install route, keep working unchanged.\n4. Declared prefixes (item 2 and the prefix half of item 3) and the judged check in a Destination version wait for the next Rules and Destination revisions that another change requires. Name both in the head report as candidates for that revision, with your publication-paths@1 encoding as the starting design. This replaces item 3 of 4fac2158: R16 brings no new Destination version.\n5. Witnesses: a publication to `.github/workflows/x.yml` is refused host-refused, with the reserved path in the answer, in a room on an older pin and in a room created from today's offer. A publication to a rules extent file is refused the same way. A publication to an ordinary path is accepted and committed. Lending's shelf pages still publish. Replay of an existing room's journal is unchanged. The install-refusal witness drops with item 2.\n6. The fold publication note's section 6 says what an application can write today: any valid path outside the reserved paths. It also says that per-application prefixes come in a later revision."}